title: After the Tribulation – End Times and Prophecy
description: End times and prophecy, post-tribulation and pre-wrath: the order of events, after the tribulation and before the wrath, the Antichrist and the beast, the day of His wrath, Gog and Magog and Ezekiel's temple, the new heavens and new earth, and watch, from the teachings on prophecy.
output: lessons/doctrine/topic-prophecy.html
highlight: tribulation; wrath

# One deck for the doctrine "End times & prophecy" (147 teachings), its themes given equal weight.
# Slide text is the author's own sentences, trimmed. The verses the teachings typed out are shown from the KJV.

=== Introduction
--- After the Tribulation [title]
overline: Doctrine · End times & prophecy
heading: After the Tribulation
sub: Christ gathers His saints after the tribulation and before God's wrath is poured out.
refs: Matthew 24:29-31; 1 Thessalonians 4:16-17; 1 Thessalonians 5:9; 2 Thessalonians 2:3; Revelation 7:14
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

# from the topic's timeline, 15186, 8156
--- The order of events
step: The tribulation | Three and a half years, 1,260 days. The beginning of sorrows; the beast rises.
step: The great tribulation | 75 days. The abomination of desolation; the beast makes war on the saints.
step: The day of the Lord | Jesus returns in the clouds and gathers the elect, the dead in Christ first, then those alive and remaining.
step: The wrath | Half an hour of silence; then 1,215 days of wrath poured out, the trumpets and the vials.
step: Armageddon and the Kingdom | The battle of Armageddon; the millennial Kingdom established.
step: The end of things | The little season, Gog and Magog; the great white throne; a new heaven and a new earth.
read: post-trib-pre-wrath-timeline | Post-Tribulation, Pre-Wrath Timeline

=== After the tribulation, before the wrath
# from 5532, 6392, 15186
--- Immediately after the tribulation
kicker: After the tribulation
big: Matthew 24:29-31 | mark: Immediately after the tribulation of those days; they shall gather together his elect
p: There is no secret rapture before the tribulation. There is a very public and unquestionable rapture before the wrath of God is poured out, after the tribulation. Dispensationalists insist the Great Tribulation occurs after a secret second coming, despite these clear verses giving the order of things.
p: *Behold, I have foretold you all things* ([[Mark 13:23]]). Pre-tribbers hate this. But Jesus was very clear, this is the order of events.

# from 7921, 7922, 7920
--- They came out of great tribulation
kicker: After the tribulation
big: Revelation 7:14 | mark: These are they which came out of great tribulation
p: Note the order. They arrive after the tribulation, after the 6 seals, on the day of the Lord. Before the wrath, which only comes after the 7th seal is opened. It is a post-trib, pre-wrath rapture.
p: The 144,000 are not modern Jews. They are 12,000 of each of the tribes, Dan swapped for Manasses, sealed on their foreheads, and left on the earth during the time of wrath, sealed against harm ([[Revelation 7:3-8]]).

# from 8103, 7896, 7835, 8085, 5555
--- The secret rapture is heresy
kicker: After the tribulation
big: Revelation 13:7 | mark: it was given unto him to make war with the saints
p: The secret pre-trib rapture, that Jesus sneaks in and quietly disappears the saved so that they don't experience the Great Tribulation, is a wicked heresy out of the pits of Hell. A secret rapture is never mentioned. *Come up hither* is John, alone and in the spirit ([[Revelation 4:1]]).
p: The false hope that we will be secretly raptured ala Left Behind is part and parcel with the lukewarm churches, the drunken watchmen, those who win no souls. Early Christians were accused of being a death cult for their lack of fear. It was faith in eternal life.

# from 9728, 5551, 6390, 5323
--- Not imminent: these come first
kicker: After the tribulation
big: 2 Thessalonians 2:3 | mark: for that day shall not come, except there come a falling away first, and that man of sin be revealed
p: The thief in the night is in reference to those caught unawares. For believers we are given what to watch for, like the fig tree. When we see the abomination of desolation stand where it ought not, we should know the day of the Lord is nigh ([[Mark 13:14]]).
p: The push for false Christianity that places salvation under the law, not under grace, the Noahide false religion, Hebrew Roots, Lordship salvation, is meant to bring about the falling away, and pave the way for the antichrist.

# from 15460, 8011, 16080, 16024
--- Spoken to believers, not to the Jews
kicker: After the tribulation
big: Luke 21:8 | mark: Take heed that ye be not deceived
p: Dispensationalists falsely claim the Olivet Discourse was “written to the Jews.” But Jesus was speaking to His disciples, believers, and made a clear distinction between “ye” and “they” in Judea. Daniel 12 and Revelation 10 are bookends ([[Daniel 12:1-2]]).
p: The mark is the means by which the beast will determine who are the saints, and make war on we who do not bow before him and worship him as God, like Shadrach, Meshach and Abednego ([[Daniel 3:17-18]]).
